# Orbit long (8–9 min)

Full steps: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §2–§4 and §7. Hooks: `FAMILIAR_DANGER_STRATEGY.md` → *Long hook*.

- **Topic:** a familiar thing in danger, with no existing public long on that subject. Run a competition check on the exact title (signed out, top five results). Fill `PRE_BUILD_VIDIQ_AUDIT.md`. **Ben picks.**
- **Script** (about 1,200–1,300 spoken words):
  - The first 3 s of picture are the danger. Sentence one is the promise, with the payoff named by 30 s.
  - 4–6 acts told as cause and effect. The world does the science; Orbit is in 1–2 beats only.
  - Picture changes every 4–6 s. Every number sourced. No goodbye; the last line hands off to the next film.
  - One `[SUBSCRIBE BEAT]` right after the first payoff (25–50% of spoken words): one line of 20 words or fewer from `templates/SUBSCRIBE_BEAT_LINES.md`, with no numbers and no stock phrases. It's gate-checked. A 4-second lower-right cue plays under it while the picture keeps moving.
  - `[VISUAL MUST]` + `[TEACH]` on every scene; `[ORBIT ACTS]` on Orbit beats only.
- **Gates:** `npm run review:script` scores 90 or more, then `npm run gate:episode` PASSes. No VO or picture spend before both.
- **Voice:** Ben Orbit Narrator (`04_Audio/tools/orbit_voice.py`). VO comes before picture. Speech around −19 to −28 dB mean; never silent.
- **Assembly:**
  - normalise inputs to 1920×1080 stereo and check A/V lengths match;
  - a remint is picture only (keep the original audio);
  - soft chapter cards with 1.5 s breath and music under;
  - an end hold of 15–20 s with a music fade (a silent hold fails);
  - export `09_Final-Export/<slug>_broadcast_v0N.mp4`.
- **Publish:** normal publish, Sunday 18:00 UK. Test & Compare with 3 thumbs; end screen = best related long + Subscribe; captions via auto-sync; a pinned comment (question + subscriber thank-you) via `scripts/update-pinned-comment.ts --create`, then pinned in Studio.
